["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>A moose trusts its nose and ears far more than its eyes. Beat the nose with wind, the ears with patience, and the eyes with stillness.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 258\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Moose senses ranked. Nose: excellent, wind at your back ends the stalk. Ears: very good, the big ears swivel and catch a snapped twig far away. Eyes: poor, they see motion but not detail. A moose often stands and stares instead of running.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"258\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Moose senses</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"78.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Nose</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"56\" width=\"222.9\" height=\"34\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"307.8571428571429\" y=\"78.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">excellent</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"134.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Ears</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"112\" width=\"178.3\" height=\"34\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"263.2857142857143\" y=\"134.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">very good</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"190.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Eyes</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"168\" width=\"66.9\" height=\"34\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"151.85714285714286\" y=\"190.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">poor: motion only</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A staring moose has seen you (hunter lore).</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Nose: excellent. Ears: very good. Eyes: poor at detail <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>The wind decides most moose hunts (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this chapter covers</summary><ul><li>The nose and how scent moves with wind and thermals, the ears and how calls carry, the eyes, how a moose combines them, and how to beat each one.</li><li>Previous: <a href=\"#/s/mc-moose-02\">Chapter 2, The body</a>. Next: <a href=\"#/s/mc-moose-04\">Chapter 4, The mind</a>.</li><li>Honest note: there is little research on moose senses. Agency summaries agree on the ranking; the details below carry their certainty (Tip where opinion).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: wind blows left to right. A hunter stands upwind. An orange scent cone grows from the hunter and widens downwind until it reaches a deer, which turns and bolts. Text: smelled you, gone. The cone widens with distance (tip).\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Your scent: a cone downwind</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"36\" width=\"400\" height=\"232\" fill=\"#e8eedc\"/>\n<path d=\"M100 197 l2 -6 M104 197 l0 -7 M108 197 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M151 206 l2 -6 M155 206 l0 -7 M159 206 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M248 129 l2 -6 M252 129 l0 -7 M256 129 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M15 239 l2 -6 M19 239 l0 -7 M23 239 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M109 153 l2 -6 M113 153 l0 -7 M117 153 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M388 187 l2 -6 M392 187 l0 -7 M396 187 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M328 188 l2 -6 M332 188 l0 -7 M336 188 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M253 141 l2 -6 M257 141 l0 -7 M261 141 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M265 129 l2 -6 M269 129 l0 -7 M273 129 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M298 204 l2 -6 M302 204 l0 -7 M306 204 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M124 124 l2 -6 M128 124 l0 -7 M132 124 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M339 187 l2 -6 M343 187 l0 -7 M347 187 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M160 234 l2 -6 M164 234 l0 -7 M168 234 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M179 253 l2 -6 M183 253 l0 -7 M187 253 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M344 134 l2 -6 M348 134 l0 -7 M352 134 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M62 151 l2 -6 M66 151 l0 -7 M70 151 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M377 182 l2 -6 M381 182 l0 -7 M385 182 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M248 163 l2 -6 M252 163 l0 -7 M256 163 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M203 175 l2 -6 M207 175 l0 -7 M211 175 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M143 203 l2 -6 M147 203 l0 -7 M151 203 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M265 143 l2 -6 M269 143 l0 -7 M273 143 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M354 201 l2 -6 M358 201 l0 -7 M362 201 l-2 -6\" stroke=\"#a9b37f\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<g><path d=\"M14 66 h44 m-9 -7 l9 7 l-9 7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;24 0;0 0\" dur=\"2s\" begin=\"0.0s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g>\n<g><path d=\"M14 150 h44 m-9 -7 l9 7 l-9 7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;24 0;0 0\" dur=\"2s\" begin=\"0.5s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g>\n<g><path d=\"M14 236 h44 m-9 -7 l9 7 l-9 7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;24 0;0 0\" dur=\"2s\" begin=\"1.0s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g>\n<rect x=\"23.2\" y=\"92.0\" width=\"49.6\" height=\"27.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"48\" y=\"111\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2c5d86\" text-anchor=\"middle\">wind</text>\n<path d=\"M112 150 L384 70 L384 230 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\"0.12\"><animate attributeName=\"d\" values=\"M112 150 L130 146 L130 154 Z;M112 150 L384 70 L384 230 Z\" dur=\"5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></path>\n<path d=\"M112 150 L384 94 L384 206 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\"0.14\"><animate attributeName=\"d\" values=\"M112 150 L130 146 L130 154 Z;M112 150 L384 94 L384 206 Z\" dur=\"5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></path>\n<path d=\"M112 150 L384 118 L384 182 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\"0.16\"><animate attributeName=\"d\" values=\"M112 150 L130 146 L130 154 Z;M112 150 L384 118 L384 182 Z\" dur=\"5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></path>\n<g transform=\"translate(100 196) scale(1.5 1.5)\"><path d=\"M-5 -20 L-6 0 M4 -20 L6 0\" stroke=\"#4a4136\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-8 -40 C-8 -44 8 -44 8 -40 L7 -19 H-7z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"-47\" r=\"5.5\" fill=\"#e0b48c\"/><path d=\"M-6 -49 C-6 -56 6 -56 6 -49z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g>\n<g><g transform=\"translate(300 198) scale(1.7 1.7)\"><path d=\"M-8 -18 L-10 0 M-4 -18 L-3 0 M12 -18 L13 0 M16 -18 L18 0\" stroke=\"#5a3e26\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-12 -28 C-12 -34 -4 -34 6 -34 C14 -34 20 -32 20 -26 C20 -20 16 -17 8 -17 L-6 -17 C-10 -17 -12 -21 -12 -28z\" fill=\"#9a7350\"/><path d=\"M-10 -30 L-16 -42 L-12 -44 L-6 -32z\" fill=\"#9a7350\"/><path d=\"M-16 -42 C-20 -43 -24 -40 -24 -38 L-20 -37 C-17 -37 -14 -39 -13 -41z\" fill=\"#9a7350\"/><path d=\"M-14 -44 L-18 -50 L-12 -45z M-12 -44 L-9 -50 L-10 -44z\" fill=\"#9a7350\"/><ellipse cx=\"18\" cy=\"-27\" rx=\"3\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#f3ead8\"/><circle cx=\"-18\" cy=\"-41\" r=\".9\" fill=\"#111\"/></g><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"4.9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"4.9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;40 -10\" begin=\"4.9s\" dur=\"0.7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><g transform=\"translate(318 198) scale(-1.7 1.7)\"><path d=\"M-8 -18 L-10 0 M-4 -18 L-3 0 M12 -18 L13 0 M16 -18 L18 0\" stroke=\"#5a3e26\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-12 -28 C-12 -34 -4 -34 6 -34 C14 -34 20 -32 20 -26 C20 -20 16 -17 8 -17 L-6 -17 C-10 -17 -12 -21 -12 -28z\" fill=\"#9a7350\"/><path d=\"M-10 -30 L-16 -42 L-12 -44 L-6 -32z\" fill=\"#9a7350\"/><path d=\"M-16 -42 C-20 -43 -24 -40 -24 -38 L-20 -37 C-17 -37 -14 -39 -13 -41z\" fill=\"#9a7350\"/><path d=\"M-14 -44 L-18 -50 L-12 -45z M-12 -44 L-9 -50 L-10 -44z\" fill=\"#9a7350\"/><ellipse cx=\"18\" cy=\"-27\" rx=\"3\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#f3ead8\"/><circle cx=\"-18\" cy=\"-41\" r=\".9\" fill=\"#111\"/></g></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"5s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"196\" y=\"234\" width=\"190\" height=\"32\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"291\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Smelled you. Gone.</text></g>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The cone widens with distance (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Your scent spreads in a cone downwind. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Smell is acute <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Your scent travels downwind in a widening cone <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the nose in detail</summary><ul><li>Minnesota Department of Natural Resources: \"Moose have rather poor eyesight, but acute senses of smell and hearing\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Guides who call moose: \"Moose trust their noses every time\" (65%, hunter forum via search; opinion).</li><li>Your scent cone starts narrow at you and widens downwind; a moose anywhere inside it can smell you (80%, <a href=\"#/s/mc-mule-deer-03\">scent and wind</a>).</li><li>A bull coming to a call often swings downwind to smell the \"cow\" before he shows (65%, Outdoor Canada; Tip). Chapter 9 shows how to set up for that.</li><li>Strong scent sources: you, your dog, your truck, your fire, your camp cooking (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation of thermals on a slope. Morning: the sun rises and warms the slope, warm air rises, and scent drifts uphill, so approach from above or the side. Evening: the sun sets, the slope cools, cool air sinks, and scent drifts downhill, so hunt from below or the side and leave before cold air drains your scent down to bedded deer.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#dbe7f3\"/>\n  <circle r=\"18\" fill=\"#f3d36b\" cx=\"40\" cy=\"250\">\n    <animate attributeName=\"cy\" values=\"250;70;70;250\" keyTimes=\"0;0.3;0.6;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <animate attributeName=\"cx\" values=\"40;80;330;370\" keyTimes=\"0;0.3;0.6;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <animate attributeName=\"fill\" values=\"#f3d36b;#f3d36b;#f2a56b;#e8590c\" keyTimes=\"0;0.5;0.8;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n  </circle>\n  <path d=\"M0 290 L0 260 Q150 240 260 120 Q300 80 400 60 L400 290 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(220 160)\"><ellipse rx=\"16\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-14\" cy=\"-7\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/></g>\n  <g stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" opacity=\"0\">\n    <animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.1;0.5;0.55;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <path d=\"M90 250 Q150 220 200 175 m-14 2 l14 -2 l-2 14\"/>\n    <path d=\"M150 260 Q220 210 270 140 m-14 2 l14 -2 l-2 14\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" opacity=\"0\">\n    <animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.6;0.65;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <path d=\"M270 120 Q220 190 160 235 m2 -14 l-2 14 l14 0\"/>\n    <path d=\"M330 100 Q280 170 230 215 m2 -14 l-2 14 l14 0\"/>\n  </g>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"36\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Morning: warm air, scent goes UP\n    <set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"4.9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#f3d36b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" opacity=\"0\">Evening: cool air, scent sinks DOWN\n    <set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"4.9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1;1;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.05;0.9;1\" begin=\"1.5s\" dur=\"3.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"96\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You: above</text></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"0\" to=\"1\" begin=\"6s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"262\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\">You: below</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Morning air rises, evening air sinks. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Morning: air warms and drifts uphill <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Evening: air cools and sinks downhill <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: thermals in moose country</summary><ul><li><button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Thermals\">Thermals</button>: sun warms slopes and air rises in the morning; at evening the air cools and drains down into valleys, wetlands and lake basins (80%, <a href=\"#/s/wind-thermals\">thermals</a>).</li><li>Wetlands and lake basins are low spots: cold evening air pools there and carries your scent down to them (Tip).</li><li>So at evening: sit beside or below the swamp with the drainage running past you, not above it at a ridge top whose air slides straight down on the moose (Tip).</li><li>Morning: approach from below or the side, as warming air lifts your scent up the slope (Tip).</li><li>Swirling wind in cutblocks and around lake edges is common; carry a wind checker and look at it every few minutes (Tip, <a href=\"#/s/wind-thermals\">wind tools</a>).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation of one day on a slope. The sun rises and crosses the sky. In the morning the sun warms the slope and blue arrows show air rising uphill. Near sunset the air swirls as the thermals switch. In the evening the slope cools and the arrows flow downhill. Morning: be above the deer. Evening: be below.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fdf1d6\"><animate attributeName=\"fill\" values=\"#fdf1d6;#fffaf0;#e9dfcf\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></rect><g><circle r=\"16\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><animateMotion dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\" keyPoints=\"0;0.8;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.4;1\" calcMode=\"linear\" path=\"M40 150 Q 200 -40 380 150\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;1;0.5\" keyTimes=\"0;0.7;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><path d=\"M0 270 L300 90 L400 90 L400 300 L0 300 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><g fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><polygon points=\"320,90 330,60 340,90\"/><polygon points=\"350,90 360,56 370,90\"/></g><g opacity=\"1\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.31;0.33;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><g><path d=\"M27.7 225.4 L68.8 200.7 M61.6 212.0 L68.8 200.7 L55.4 201.8\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M117.7 171.4 L158.8 146.7 M151.6 158.0 L158.8 146.7 L145.4 147.8\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M207.7 117.4 L248.8 92.7 M241.6 104.0 L248.8 92.7 L235.4 93.8\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;22.3 -13.4\" dur=\"1.5s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g><text x=\"12\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Morning: sun warms the slope</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">Air rises UPHILL</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.31;0.33;0.65;0.67;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><g stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M90 200 c 20 -30, 50 -10, 30 10 c -15 15, -30 -5, -15 -15\"/><path d=\"M200 140 c -20 -30, -50 -10, -30 10 c 15 15, 30 -5, 15 -15\"/></g><text x=\"12\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Near sunset: the switch</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">Air swirls, mixed</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.65;0.67;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><g><path d=\"M68.8 200.7 L27.7 225.4 M41.0 224.4 L27.7 225.4 L34.9 214.1\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M158.8 146.7 L117.7 171.4 M131.0 170.4 L117.7 171.4 L124.9 160.1\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M248.8 92.7 L207.7 117.4 M221.0 116.4 L207.7 117.4 L214.9 106.1\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;-22.3 13.4\" dur=\"1.5s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g><text x=\"12\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Evening: slope cools</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">Air sinks DOWNHILL</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.65;0.67;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"190\" y=\"230\" width=\"200\" height=\"56\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"290\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Morning: be above</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Evening: be below</text></g></svg>\n<figcaption>The day on a slope: up in the morning, down at evening. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 290\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A moose with sound waves spreading out. A cow moose rutting moan can be heard up to 3 kilometres away. The big ears turn toward sound. Calls carry best on calm, cool days.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"290\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ears: a call carries 3 km</text><g transform=\"translate(70 170) scale(0.8)\"><rect x=\"-36\" y=\"4\" width=\"8\" height=\"52\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#9c8a76\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"-26\" y=\"4\" width=\"8\" height=\"52\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#9c8a76\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"26\" y=\"4\" width=\"8\" height=\"52\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#9c8a76\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"36\" y=\"4\" width=\"8\" height=\"52\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#9c8a76\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M-46 0 Q-48 -26 -20 -26 Q10 -40 34 -34 Q48 -26 44 2 Q20 22 -30 18 Q-48 16 -46 0 Z\" fill=\"#3b2a1c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M30 -30 L56 -40 L66 -26 L40 0 Z\" fill=\"#3b2a1c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M56 -44 L86 -30 Q92 -22 84 -18 L64 -20 Q54 -26 56 -44 Z\" fill=\"#3b2a1c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M66 -22 Q66 -6 60 -4 Q58 -12 62 -22 Z\" fill=\"#3b2a1c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"54\" cy=\"-50\" rx=\"8\" ry=\"3.5\" transform=\"rotate(-30 54 -50)\" fill=\"#3b2a1c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"-34\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#eeeeee\"/></g><path d=\"M150 120 Q260 80 380 120\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 6\"/><path d=\"M150 132 Q163 150 150 168\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M180 114 Q196 150 180 186\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M210 96 Q229 150 210 204\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"270\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">cow moan: up to 3 km</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Big ears turn to sound (Tip)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"249\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Calls carry best on calm, cool days</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A bull may answer from far off</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>A cow's rut moan carries up to 3 km <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Calls carry best on calm, cool days <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: hearing in detail</summary><ul><li>BC account <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>: \"At rutting time, cow Moose emit a long, quavering moan that is audible for up to 3 km. This call can attract a bull or bulls in forested terrain where visual contact is limited.\"</li><li>Hearing is acute (75%, Minnesota Department of Natural Resources). No moose hearing range study was found: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> numbers in Hz.</li><li>Outdoor Canada <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>: cool, clear, calm days or a light breeze are best for calling; heavy wind or rain muddies calls.</li><li>Moose make plenty of noise themselves: snapping branches, splashing, grunts, raking brush. A careful, irregular step with pauses can pass for a moose; a steady human rhythm cannot (Tip).</li><li>Metal on metal, voices and car doors are the giveaways (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 310\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Top view of a moose head with eyes set on the sides, giving a wide view all around and a small blind spot straight behind. Moose pick up motion but see still shapes poorly.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"310\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Eyes on the side of the head</text><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"170\" r=\"110\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M200 170 L200 60 A110 110 0 1 1 199 60 Z\" fill=\"#c9d6b0\"/><path d=\"M200 170 L186 282 A110 110 0 0 0 214 282 Z\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"170\" rx=\"18\" ry=\"30\" fill=\"#3b2a1c\"/><circle cx=\"184\" cy=\"160\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#eee\"/><circle cx=\"216\" cy=\"160\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#eee\"/><path d=\"M190 140 L200 120 L210 140 Z\" fill=\"#3b2a1c\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">wide side view</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">small blind spot behind</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Motion: yes</text><text x=\"392\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Still shapes: poor</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Poor at still shapes; quick to see motion <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Freeze when it looks. Move when it feeds (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: vision in detail</summary><ul><li>Agency summaries call moose eyesight \"rather poor\" (75%, Minnesota Department of Natural Resources).</li><li>Eyes on the side of the head give a wide view and a small blind spot behind (75%, general deer family anatomy; moose specific degrees: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li><li>Like other deer family members, moose likely see blue and yellow better than red; blaze orange looks dull to them (60%, Tip, based on deer research). The law on blaze orange: see the Rule Book.</li><li>Low light: they are active at dawn and dusk, so their eyes work well in poor light (Tip).</li><li>What it means for you: stand still and a moose may look straight at you and not know what you are; move and it will (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-moose-bull-front.jpg\" alt=\"Bull moose, front view, Grand Teton. Antlers spread wide like two open hands; heavy bulbous nose.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Bull moose, front view, Grand Teton. Antlers spread wide like two open hands; heavy bulbous nose. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: GrandTetonNPS, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bull_Moose_Sticking_Tongue_Out_(28257188958).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>A staring moose has noticed you (Tip).</li><li>It may stand for long seconds before it moves (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what the stare means</summary><ul><li>Hunter wisdom: a moose often stands and stares instead of running. Do not read that as \"it has not seen me\" (60%, hunter lore, <a href=\"#/s/moose\">Moose</a>).</li><li>Use the stare: if you are already set and the moose is a legal bull, broadside, with a clear backstop, the stare can be your shot (Tip).</li><li>If it is a cow with a calf, or a bull with ears back, the stare can turn into a charge. Chapter 4 has the warning signs.</li><li>Never shoot a moose only because it stands still. Count first (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calling setup seen from above, all tips. The wind blows from the calling bull toward you. The shooter sits in front with an open shooting lane on the downwind side, and the caller sits behind. Bulls often circle downwind to smell the call before they show, so watch that side.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Calling setup, seen from above (Tip)</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"260\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".6\"/><polygon points=\"31.0,80 40,53.0 49.0,80\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"38.2\" y=\"80\" width=\"3.6\" height=\"5.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><polygon points=\"61.0,70 70,43.0 79.0,70\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"68.2\" y=\"70\" width=\"3.6\" height=\"5.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><polygon points=\"51.0,110 60,83.0 69.0,110\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"58.2\" y=\"110\" width=\"3.6\" height=\"5.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><polygon points=\"361.0,200 370,173.0 379.0,200\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"368.2\" y=\"200\" width=\"3.6\" height=\"5.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><polygon points=\"341.0,222 350,195.0 359.0,222\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"348.2\" y=\"222\" width=\"3.6\" height=\"5.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><g transform=\"translate(300 92) scale(0.45 0.45)\"><rect x=\"-32\" y=\"6\" width=\"7\" height=\"44\" rx=\"3.5\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"-22\" y=\"6\" width=\"7\" height=\"44\" rx=\"3.5\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"24\" y=\"6\" width=\"7\" height=\"44\" rx=\"3.5\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"33\" y=\"6\" width=\"7\" height=\"44\" rx=\"3.5\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"44\" ry=\"18\" fill=\"#c8a26b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"-38\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"9\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#f1e3c0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M26 -12 L44 -44 L58 -40 L42 8 Z\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"60\" cy=\"-44\" rx=\"15\" ry=\"7\" transform=\"rotate(20 60 -44)\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"46\" cy=\"-54\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"3.5\" transform=\"rotate(-35 46 -54)\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M50 -50 Q36 -80 6 -100 M48 -56 L60 -66 M46 -62 L58 -74 M38 -76 L44 -92 M28 -86 L30 -102 M18 -93 L18 -106\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></g><text x=\"300\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Calling bull</text><path d=\"M300 110 Q240 170 150 200 Q120 210 110 240\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 6\"/><text x=\"236\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Bulls often circle</text><text x=\"236\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">downwind (Tip)</text><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"232\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"194\" y=\"238\" width=\"12\" height=\"16\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Shooter</text><circle cx=\"260\" cy=\"265.8\" r=\"5.4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"254.6\" y=\"271.2\" width=\"10.8\" height=\"14.4\" rx=\"3.6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><text x=\"280\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Caller behind</text><path d=\"M170 56 L134 112\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M135.1 103.1 L134.0 112.0 L141.7 107.3\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M110 84 L74 140\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M75.1 131.1 L74.0 140.0 L81.7 135.3\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">Wind</text><path d=\"M200 230 L160 200\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\">lane</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Ears hear, nose confirms, eyes check last (Tip).</li><li>A sound with no smell makes it curious; smell makes it leave (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: combining the senses</summary><ul><li>Typical order (Tip, hunter consensus): a sound turns the ears; the moose then tries to get the wind; it looks last.</li><li>A bull that hears a call and cannot see a moose may \"clam up and circle downwind\" (60%, hunter forum via search; Tip).</li><li>Over calling when a bull is close lets him pinpoint you; if he cannot see a moose he may hang up or circle (60%, Tip).</li><li>A wrong smell usually ends it at once; a wrong sound or shape may only make it wait and watch (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Sense</th><th>Beat it by</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nose</td><td>Wind in your face; thermals in mind <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Ears</td><td>Few sounds, moose like rhythm, no metal (Tip)</td></tr><tr><td>Eyes</td><td>Freeze when it looks; move when it feeds (Tip)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, seen from above: wind blows from the deer toward the hunter. The hunter walks a curved path upwind, keeping the wind in their face, and stops behind a tree in range. A scent cone trails behind the hunter, away from the deer. Final label: in range, hidden.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#e7ecdc\"/>\n<path d=\"M96 289 l2 -6 M100 289 l0 -7 M104